### ============================================
### WEBSERV: FILE UPLOAD HANDLER TEST SUITE
### ============================================
### Description: Tests for multipart/form-data file uploads.
### Assumes a server on port 8080 with a location like:
###   location /upload/ {
###       allow_methods POST;
###       root /var/www/uploads;
###       client_max_body_size 5M;
###   }
### Also assumes you have a directory `tests/upload_files/` with:
###   - small.txt
###   - image.png
###   - empty.txt
### ============================================

### Variables
@host = localhost
@port = 8080
@baseUrl = http://{{host}}:{{port}}
@userAgent = WebServ-Test-Client/1.0
@boundary = ----WebAppBoundaryABC123

### ============================================
### Section 1: Successful Uploads
### ============================================

### Test 1.1: Upload a small text file
# Expects: 201 Created with a success HTML page.
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="small.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a small test file for upload.

--{{boundary}}--

### Test 1.2: Upload a binary file (image)
# Expects: 201 Created.
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="image.png"
Content-Type: image/png

<@ ./tests/upload_files/image.png
--{{boundary}}--

### Test 1.3: Upload a file with a name to be sanitized
# Filename has spaces and special characters.
# Expects: 201 Created. The file on the server should be named something like "file_with_spaces___and_chars.txt".
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="file with spaces &@!.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Testing filename sanitization.
--{{boundary}}--

### Test 1.4: Upload an empty file
# Expects: 201 Created. The server should create an empty file.
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="empty.txt"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

<@ ./tests/upload_files/empty.txt
--{{boundary}}--

### ============================================
### Section 2: Client Error Handling (4xx)
### ============================================

### Test 2.1: Missing Content-Type header
# The handler requires a Content-Type.
# Expects: 415 Unsupported Media Type
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Length: 100

Some data.

### Test 2.2: Incorrect Content-Type header
# The handler requires multipart/form-data.
# Expects: 415 Unsupported Media Type
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 18

{"key": "value"}

### Test 2.3: Missing boundary in Content-Type
# The multipart parser needs a boundary to work.
# Expects: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data
Content-Length: 100

--boundary
...
--boundary--

### Test 2.4: Missing Content-Length header
# Uploads must have a Content-Length.
# Expects: 411 Length Required (or 400 Bad Request depending on server strictness)
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

data
--{{boundary}}--

### Test 2.5: Malformed multipart body (no closing boundary)
# The parser should time out or detect an error.
# Expects: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="malformed.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This request is intentionally broken and will not be closed properly.

### Test 2.6: Upload exceeds client_max_body_size
# Assumes client_max_body_size is set to a small value like 1K for this test.
# Expects: 413 Payload Too Large
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload/
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="large_file.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a large block of text designed to exceed a small client_max_body_size limit.
... (repeat this line many times) ...
This is a large block of text designed to exceed a small client_max_body_size limit.
--{{boundary}}--

### ============================================
### Section 3: Redirects
### ============================================

### Test 3.1: Request to upload location without trailing slash
# The handler should redirect to add the slash.
# Expects: 301 Moved Permanently, Location: /upload/
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}
Content-Length: 150

--{{boundary}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="redirect_test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

test
--{{boundary}}--
```// filepath: tests/upload_handler_tests.http
